# Inventory Management System

A Python-based Inventory Management System built using Object-Oriented Programming (OOP), file handling, and a modular project structure.

## Features

* Add new items
* View all items
* Search items
* Remove items
* Update item prices
* Update item quantities
* Inventory summary
* Automatic file saving
* Automatic file loading on startup

## Technologies Used

* Python
* OOP (Classes and Objects)
* File Handling
* Modular Programming

## Project Structure

```text
Inventory Management System
│
├── main.py
├── classfile.py
├── function.py
├── utils.py
├── file_handling.py
└── Inventory.txt
```

## How It Works

Each item is stored as an object containing:

* Name
* Price
* Quantity

The inventory stores and manages all item objects.

Data is saved into a text file and automatically loaded when the program starts.

## Features Implemented

### CRUD Operations

* Create Item
* Read Item
* Update Item
* Delete Item

### Inventory Analysis

* Search items
* Calculate total inventory value
* Count total items

